1
00:00:00,706 --> 00:00:02,265
Americans spent more,

2
00:00:02,399 --> 00:00:06,094
but inflation erased the gain in after-tax income.

3
00:00:07,276 --> 00:00:10,555
Today's federal report puts annual price growth at

4
00:00:10,663 --> 00:00:12,545
three point four percent,

5
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:15,100
above the Fed's two percent goal.

6
00:00:17,195 --> 00:00:19,758
After-tax income rose in August.

7
00:00:20,039 --> 00:00:21,518
Prices rose, too,

8
00:00:21,679 --> 00:00:23,532
leaving buying power flat.

9
00:00:23,866 --> 00:00:25,184
Spending still grew,

10
00:00:25,372 --> 00:00:27,122
even after inflation.

11
00:00:28,302 --> 00:00:29,378
The next test:

12
00:00:29,539 --> 00:00:32,135
can income start outpacing prices?

13
00:00:32,516 --> 00:00:35,541
That's what gives households more room to breathe.
